2.—(1) In these Regulations —
“appropriate form”, in relation to any provision of these Regulations, means the form set out for the purposes of that provision on the Internet website at https://mha.gov.sg/mha‑e‑services;
“authorised representative”, in relation to an entity making representations under section 16(2) or an application under section 17(2) or 32(2)(b), means the responsible officer of the entity authorised by the entity to make the representations or application, as the case may be;
“constitutional documents”, in relation to an entity, means the constitution, memorandum or articles of association, trust deed or equivalent instrument of the entity;
“contact address”, for any person, means either or both of the following nominated by the person for the service of documents on that person:
(a)an address in Singapore;
(b)an email address;
“donations report”, in relation to a reporting period, means a report made under section 18(1) of all reportable donations for the reporting period;
“foreign affiliations report”, in relation to a reporting period, means a report made under section 19(1) of all of the designated entity’s foreign affiliations for the reporting period;
“identity particulars” means —
(a)for an individual, the individual’s —
(i)full name;
(ii)identity card number, passport number or work pass number;
(iii)nationality and date of birth; and
(iv)contact address; or
(b)for an entity, the entity’s —
(i)full name;
(ii)country of incorporation or formation;
(iii)Unique Entity Number (UEN), if any; and
(iv)contact address;
“key management report” means a report made under section 20(1) of a designated entity’s governing body composition;
“market value”, in relation to any property, means the price that the property might reasonably be expected to fetch on a sale in the open market;
“property” does not include money;
“reportable donation”, in relation to a reporting period, means any foreign donation or anonymous donation accepted by a designated entity during that period, excluding any donations that need not be reported under regulation 11;
“reportable foreign affiliation”, in relation to a reporting period, means any foreign affiliation that a designated entity has during that period;
“reporting period” means —
(a)for reportable donations — the period described in regulation 10; or
(b)for reportable foreign affiliations — the period described in regulation 17.
(2) Unless it is otherwise provided, a reference to a section in these Regulations is a reference to a section in the Act.

4.—(1) For the purposes of section 13(2)(h), a payment of money to an entity is a “donation” to the entity if the payment is made for any consideration whose market value is lower than the value of the money.
(2) For the purposes of section 13(2)(i), each of the following is a “donation” to an entity:
(a)a gift of property to the entity;
(b)a transfer of property to the entity for any consideration in money given by the entity, but only if the value of the money is lower than the market value of the property;
(c)a transfer of property to the entity for any consideration (other than money) given by the entity, but only if the market value of the consideration is lower than the market value of the property;
(d)the provision of any services to the entity otherwise than on commercial terms.

12. A donations report for a reporting period must report the following matters for each reportable donation accepted during that period:
(a)if the reportable donation is a foreign donation — the foreign principal’s identity particulars;
(b)if the reportable donation is an anonymous donation and the donation is made through a third party (such as a payment service provider as defined by section 2(1) of the Payment Services Act 2019) — the third party’s identity particulars;
(c)for a donation of money in Singapore dollars — the sum donated;
(d)for a donation of money in other currencies — the sum donated and the equivalent in Singapore dollars when the donation was accepted;
(e)for a donation other than of money — the estimated market value of the donation;
(f)how the donation was made;
(g)when the donation was received and accepted;
(h)the particular purpose for which the donation was made, if any.

18. A foreign affiliations report for a reporting period must report the following matters for each foreign affiliation during that period:
(a)a description of the arrangement or agreement between the designated entity and the foreign principal, including —
(i)how the arrangement or agreement started;
(ii)when the arrangement or agreement started; and
(iii)if the arrangement or agreement ended during the reporting period — when the arrangement or agreement ended;
(b)the foreign principal’s identity particulars.
